  "step_3": "The information relevant to the decision reason — the most favorable outcome with the lowest probability — is not considered by the individual. The individual focuses only on the overall probability of winning (34% vs. 33%), not on the specific comparison of the least probable outcomes. The decision reason requires comparing the value of the outcome with the smallest probability: in B, 2500 Euros at 33%; in A, 2400 Euros at 34%. Since 33% < 34%, B has the lower probability, and 2500 > 2400, so B has the more favorable least probable outcome. Therefore, the reason would prefer B. However, the individual chose A based on higher probability, not on the value of the least probable outcome. The justification does not reflect the rule of the decision reason. Thus, the individual did not use the decision reason. The reasoning is entirely different and based on a different criterion (probability of winning, not value of least probable outcome).",
  "final_assessment_score": 0
